        "titulo": "Pocket summary",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: • 1. An adjective completes a noun. It is root + ending. STEP 2: • 2. The root never changes. The ending changes to agree. STEP 3: • 3. You only memorise the masculine. The other three forms come for free. STEP 4: • 4. The \"scissors\": cut the last two letters of the masculine, paste the new ending. STEP 5: • 5. Three masculine endings: STEP 6: -ЫЙ (common) STEP 7: -ОЙ (stress on the ending) STEP 8: -ИЙ (after г, к, х, ж, ч, ш, щ or the синий family) STEP 9: • 6. Feminine endings: -АЯ (common) or -ЯЯ (синий family). STEP 10: • 7. Neuter endings: -ОЕ (common) or -ЕЕ (синий family). STEP 11: • 8. The синий family is the only real exception: си́ний → си́няя → си́нее → си́ние. STEP 12: • 9. Adjectives in -ИЙ after г, к, х, ж, ч, ш, щ are not from the синий family: ру́сский → ру́сская, хоро́ший → хоро́шая. STEP 13: • 10. The stress can wander: большо́й → больша́я → большо́е. Do not try to guess. Copy it from the table. STEP 14: • 11. Э́то never changes and replaces the verb «to be» in the present.",
